---
import CommercialLayout from '../../components/CommercialLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../data/site';

const canonical = `${SITE.url}/privacy/`;
const updated = '10 September 2026';
---

<CommercialLayout
  title={`Privacy policy · ${SITE.name}`}
  description="What OperStack collects on oper-stack.com, why, where it goes, how long it stays, and how to ask for a copy or deletion."
  canonical={canonical}
>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Last updated {updated}</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      What OperStack collects when you use this site, why, where it goes, how long it stays, and how to ask for a copy or deletion.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      OperStack (oper-stack.com) is a trading name used by Maksim Shchegolev, who operates it as a sole trader from Argentina.
      Questions about this policy go to <a href="mailto:legal@oper-stack.com">legal@oper-stack.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>What</th><th>When</th><th>Why</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Name, email, phone or WhatsApp number, your message, the page you sent it from</td>
          <td>When you send a form: an audit request, a product order, a PDF request</td>
          <td>To answer you, confirm scope and deliver what you asked for</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>The site URL you type into the AI visibility check</td>
          <td>When you run the check</td>
          <td>To fetch and score public pages of that site. The score is cached for ten minutes, then discarded</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Order details: product, plan, price, receipt number, the email on the order</td>
          <td>When you buy a paid product</td>
          <td>To issue the licence key, give support and handle refunds. Card details go to the merchant of record and never reach us</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Usage data: pages viewed, approximate location, device and browser, referring site</td>
          <td>While you browse, through Google Analytics 4</td>
          <td>To see which pages work and fix the ones that do not</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Technical logs: IP address, user agent, request time</td>
          <td>On every request, kept by our hosting provider</td>
          <td>Security and error diagnosis</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Where the data goes</h2>
    <p>
      Form submissions reach us in three places: the OperStack mailbox on Google Workspace, a private Telegram notification, and our lead
      database in Notion. Paid orders are processed by a merchant of record (Paddle, Lemon Squeezy or Whop, named on your receipt), which
      keeps the payment record under its own privacy policy. The site is hosted on Vercel; analytics run on Google Analytics 4.
    </p>
    <p>We do not sell personal data and we do not share it with advertisers.</p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Form submissions and lead records: until the request is closed, and for up to two years after the last contact, unless a contract requires longer.</li>
      <li>Order records: for as long as tax law requires the merchant of record and us to keep invoices.</li>
      <li>AI visibility results: ten minutes in a cache, then gone. Nothing is stored unless you request the PDF and leave an email.</li>
      <li>Analytics: under the retention settings of our Google Analytics property. You can opt out with the Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on or by blocking cookies.</li>
      <li>Server logs: for the short period our hosting provider keeps them.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      The site sets Google Analytics cookies (names starting with <code>_ga</code>) to tell returning visitors from new ones. There are no
      advertising cookies. Blocking cookies in your browser does not break the site.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Wherever you live, you can ask what we hold about you, have it corrected, or have it deleted, and you can object to analytics
      processing. Write to <a href="mailto:legal@oper-stack.com">legal@oper-stack.com</a> from the address you used with us; we answer within
      30 days. If you live in the EU, the UK, Brazil, California or another place with its own privacy law, the rights that law gives you apply
      in addition.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The site and the products are for businesses and professionals. We do not knowingly collect data from anyone under 16.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>When this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it. Material changes are announced on this page for 30 days.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Privacy questions: <a href="mailto:legal@oper-stack.com">legal@oper-stack.com</a>. Everything else:
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>
    <p><a href="/terms/">Terms of service</a> · <a href="/refunds/">Refund policy</a></p>
  </div>
</CommercialLayout>

<style>
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--fm);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  code {
    font-family: var(--fm);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--teal-soft);
  }
</style>
